10.text:
PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
The group maintains complete unanimous consensus on D (Sepsis) as the definitive etiology of the patient's acute respiratory failure. The 29-day postoperative interval strictly excludes acute transfusion reactions and perioperative myocardial necrosis, which manifest within hours to days rather than weeks later. Late complications following a Whipple procedure, such as occult anastomotic breakdown or intra-abdominal abscesses, typically declare at this stage, leading to sepsis-induced Acute Respiratory Distress Syndrome.
}

